---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/about.css';
---
<Layout title="About the Maker & Our Guides | Teleprompter Pal" description="Meet Thomas Lee, maker of Teleprompter Pal and Free Teleprompter Online. Read about his background, the tools he builds and how to get in touch.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="about-page container" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/AboutPage">
    <link itemprop="url" href="https://teleprompterpal.com/about/" />
    <nav class="about-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">About</span></nav>
    <header class="about-intro"><h1 itemprop="name">About Teleprompter Pal</h1>
      <p class="about-lead" itemprop="description">An iPhone teleprompter, made by Thomas Lee.</p>
      <p>Teleprompter Pal brings your script, recording and basic edit into one workflow. I also make <a href="https://freeteleprompteronline.com/">Free Teleprompter Online</a>, a browser reader you can use without installing an app.</p>
    </header>
    <figure class="about-portrait"><img src="/images/about/thomas-lee-watercolor-1200.webp" srcset="/images/about/thomas-lee-watercolor-480.webp 480w, /images/about/thomas-lee-watercolor-800.webp 800w, /images/about/thomas-lee-watercolor-1200.webp 1200w" sizes="(min-width: 960px) 800px, (max-width: 767px) calc(100vw - 48px), 704px" width="1200" height="676" alt="Watercolor illustration of Thomas Lee in glasses and a navy shirt, working at a desk with a laptop." loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" /></figure>
    <section aria-labelledby="maker"><h2 id="maker">Who makes it</h2>
      <p>I’m <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thomas-lee-9733b0343/" rel="me">Thomas Lee</a>, the maker behind Teleprompter Pal and Free Teleprompter Online. I publish both products through Second Wind, LLC.</p>
      <p>The two tools serve different recording setups. Teleprompter Pal keeps the script and camera workflow together on an iPhone. Free Teleprompter Online gives you a reader at your computer. When I recommend one from the other, I’m recommending a product I also make.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="background"><h2 id="background">My background</h2>
      <p>I’m also the founder of Georamp, where my work focuses on AI search visibility: how brands are mentioned, cited and recommended across tools such as ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Perplexity. You can find that work and my professional background on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thomas-lee-9733b0343/">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
      <p>Teleprompter Pal addresses another part of communication: getting words from a script into a video. The focus here is on the practical work of preparing, rehearsing, recording and finishing a take.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="purpose"><h2 id="purpose">Why this app</h2>
      <p>A script should help you speak, without pulling all your attention toward reading it. Teleprompter Pal puts the words near the camera, lets you set a comfortable scrolling pace and keeps your retakes with the script.</p>
      <p>You can write or import your words, rehearse, record while reading, then trim, crop and export an MP4. Your original recording stays in the library when you edit a copy. The <a href="/guides/record-video-with-script-iphone/">iPhone recording guide</a> walks through that whole path, including checking the saved file.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="building"><h2 id="building">How the tools are built</h2>
      <p>The app’s writing, rehearsal, recording and editing workflow runs on your iPhone without an account. Scripts and original recordings stay on the device. You decide where an exported copy goes.</p>
      <p>Teleprompter Pal supports iPhone with iOS 18 or later and uses scrolling controls you set yourself. For a browser setup, <a href="/guides/browser-teleprompter-vs-iphone-app/">compare the two workflows</a> before choosing where to record.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="editorial" aria-labelledby="editorial-title"><h2 id="editorial-title">About the guides</h2>
      <p>The “Teleprompter Pal team” byline identifies this site’s publisher. I’m responsible for its content. I use AI assistance for research, drafting and illustrations, and link to the documentation, original research and testing notes that support the advice.</p>
      <p>Illustrations explain a setup; they are not evidence of a real recording. Dated test notes distinguish physical-device checks from Simulator, desktop and synthetic tests. Original publication dates stay in place, and substantive changes receive an update note.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="corrections" aria-labelledby="contact-title"><h2 id="contact-title">Get in touch</h2>
      <p>If something is broken, a guide needs correcting or you have a question, email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>. Include the page or app version and what happened. Please leave private scripts and recordings out unless they are needed and you choose to share them.</p>
      <p><a href={site.supportUrl}>Get product support</a>, read the <a href={site.privacyUrl}>privacy policy</a> or <a href="/#app-updates">get Teleprompter Pal updates</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
